{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula","id":1121176,"title":"How to Stat Dracula","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-26T21:17:38-07:00","id":1121176,"title":"How to Stat Dracula","content":"Hello. What sorts of powers and stats would you give Dracula in the modern day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T21:36:50-07:00","id":1121183,"title":"","content":"I generally wouldn't stat Dracula for the sole purpose of if it has stats then it can be beaten.<br /> <br /> However, if I was statting Dracula then I would make him the vampire equivalent of an Archmage or Incarnate, and I'd give him five dots in all the coils.<br /> <br /> After that then I would just start giving him dots in disciplines that I felt worked; Protean and Animalism are definite musts, and the physical disciplines make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> I would also give him dots in Cruac because of it's powers to form storms.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, take your pick of the other disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T21:58:37-07:00","id":1121189,"title":"","content":"He's definitely got Protean 5 (he turns into mist). Animalism at least 1 and probably more like 5 (he influences wolves, arguably more than one at a time, and could easily be argued to have the grounds around his castle under the effects of Lord of the Land). Obfuscate at least 1 and probably more like 4 (he hides himself from sight, and changes his appearance a few times, although it could be argued the latter is mundane disguise). Dominate at least 2 and probably closer to 4 (he controls a few people's minds, in particular Renfield seems to be under longer-term control, and while that could just be the effects of the blood bond, it could also be argued to be Iron Edict or even Conditioning). It's difficult to assess if he would have Auspex, Majesty, or Nightmare and at what levels. He's definitely alluring, frightening, and prescient, but whether mundanely or supernaturally so is difficult to say, and it's harder to pick out specific moments and say &quot;that has to be this level of this power.&quot; Not sure what level Cruac a weather control ritual would be, but he's definitely got that. It's pretty much impossible to determine his levels of the physical disciplines, but he clearly has all three in some measure. In CofD, he'd presumably have all three of the standard Coils at high levels, considering he allegedly invented them; Ascendant in particular he either has above 5 or has some kind of crazy Scale for, because he walks in the sun unprotected and unharmed, if perhaps not at full strength. And that's just his Disciplines. I'm pretty sure he'd easily break 500 experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:03:58-07:00","id":1121190,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Dracula</b><br /> <br /> That will depend entirely on what sort of Dracula you want to use. The character has been interpreted, re-interpreted and re-invented endlessly so there is no one &quot;definitive&quot; version of the character. I would say decide the role you want him to play in your game and build accordingly.<br /> <br /> I will post the version I use in my games below. Using the Dracula, Prince of Paris plot hook from the <i>Chroniclers Guide</i> as inspiration, this version has ruled the City of Lights for over 100 years under an alias. His use of the coils has pushed him beyond the limitations of clans and he is considered clanless (although as the Prince of Paris he poses as a Gangrel). He is careful not to expose the true extent for his power, lest others discover who is truly is.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Vlad Dracul \u2013 Dracula</b></span><br /> <b>Mask: </b>Master; <b>Dirge: </b>Philosopher<br /> <b>Clan</b>: Unknown<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Unaligned<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 6, Wits 5, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 6<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 4, Composure 6<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Academics 5(History, Religion), Animal Ken 5 (Children of the Night), Athletics 4, Brawl 4, Crafts 2, Expression 3 (Writing), Intimidation 6(Terror), Investigation 5 (Supernatural Mysteries), Medicine 3, Persuasion 5, Occult 6 (Transcendence), Politics 5 (Ordo Dracul), Ride 4, Science 3 (Experimentation), Socialize 5, Survival 4(Transylvania), Stealth 5, Subterfuge 5(Occult Secrets), Warfare 4, Weaponry 5(Halberd, Sword)<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Acute Senses, Allies (Many), Area of Expertise (Ordo Dracul, Transcendence), Around the Block, Claws of the Unholy, Contacts (Many), Cutthroat, Defensive Combat (Weaponry), Eidetic Memory, Etiquette 5, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Occult), Eye for the Strange, Fame 3, Haven 5, Herd 5, Indomitable, Inspiring, Iron Will, Language (Many), Meditative Mind 4, Professional Training 4 (Voivode; Persuasion, Politics, Warfare), Resources 5, Retainer 5,Safe Place 5, Status 5 (Prince of Paris), Striking Looks 1, Style: Armed Defense 3, Style: Heavy Weapons 4, Style: Kindred Dueling 4, Style: Mounted Combat 1, Style: Riding the Wave 5, Style: Weapon and Shield 2, Swarm Form, Taste, Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer 1, Undeniable Aura<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism 5, Auspex 5, Celerity 3, Dominate 4, Majesty 5, Nightmare 4, Obfuscate 4, Protean 5, Resilience 4, Vigor 4<br /> <b>Blood Magic: </b>Cruac 3 (Cheval, Deflection of Wooden Doom, Drops of Destiny, Touch of the Morrigan), Theban 3 (Damned Radiance, Malediction of Despair, Sanctity, Vitae Reliquary)<br /> <b>Devotions: </b>Annals of Death, Force of Nature, Legion, Quicken Sight, Shared Sight, Summoning, Vermin Flood<br /> <b>Coils: </b>Ascendant 5, Quintessence 5, Voivode 5, Wyrm 5, and likely more<br /> <b>Humanity:</b> 5<br /> <b>Blood Potency</b>: 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Health:</b> 11 - </span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:16:37-07:00","id":1121194,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/65829/Night-Horrors-Count-F-Dracula?\" target=\"_blank\">Here you go</a>.<br /> <br /> But seriously, he seems more like a mobile guy than he is usually depicted. Or was, I guess. Like, if he 'lived' in his castle, you have to imagine everyone would go see him, or die trying to. To any vampire hunter, he's got to be the biggest and most well-known name on the list. And of course any enemy of the Ordo Dracul would love to rip the secrets out of him, or just eliminate him as a claim to fame. Plus he potentially has God-Machine agents after him.<br /> <br /> Count Motherfucking Dracula always said it was an inherited title, but I don't think it meant 'the' Dracula was dead.<br /> <br /> In the Danse Macabre, we have the Dragon's Eye, a 'gonzo' version of the Ordo Dracul that I think was sort of combined with it to make the second edition Ordo. It says he occasionally visits their lairs, checks up on their research. It also says this, 'Thing is, Dracul doesn\u2019t consider himself a vampire anymore. He thinks he\u2019s transcended that. In fact, he can walk out in the day time, stakes don\u2019t bother him, and most of the other restrictions have fallen away like dry scabs. Problem is, the conspiracy doesn\u2019t yet know how to replicate it. The Coils are the closest they can get to cracking the powers that Dracul possesses.'<br /> <br /> So why not? Powerful vampire, none of the vampire weaknesses. Just stuck with immortality and an eternal search for something else.<br /> <br /> You might check <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1591/Rites-of-the-Dragon?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> for personality, if interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-27-2017, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:54:06-07:00","id":1121203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula?p=1121194#post1121194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Danse Macabre, we have the Dragon's Eye, a 'gonzo' version of the Ordo Dracul that I think was sort of combined with it to make the second edition Ordo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Side note - is it just me, or does it seem like they did a bit of that with all of the Covenants in 2e? It's most obvious with the Ordo and the Crone, the latter even gaining its gonzo version's name as one of its nicknames. But to me it seems like they all took a little bit of inspiration from their Danse Macabre equivalents for their 2e updates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T23:29:55-07:00","id":1121207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula#post1121176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. What sorts of powers and stats would you give Dracula in the modern day?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very poor stats, with devotions he cant use and a build that any decent combat oriented PC could kick his ass with. Oh i was beaten to the punchline with that one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula?p=1121189#post1121189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's definitely got Protean 5 (he turns into mist). Animalism at least 1 and probably more like 5 (he influences wolves, arguably more than one at a time, and could easily be argued to have the grounds around his castle under the effects of Lord of the Land). Obfuscate at least 1 and probably more like 4 (he hides himself from sight, and changes his appearance a few times, although it could be argued the latter is mundane disguise). Dominate at least 2 and probably closer to 4 (he controls a few people's minds, in particular Renfield seems to be under longer-term control, and while that could just be the effects of the blood bond, it could also be argued to be Iron Edict or even Conditioning). It's difficult to assess if he would have Auspex, Majesty, or Nightmare and at what levels. He's definitely alluring, frightening, and prescient, but whether mundanely or supernaturally so is difficult to say, and it's harder to pick out specific moments and say &quot;that has to be this level of this power.&quot; Not sure what level Cruac a weather control ritual would be, but he's definitely got that. It's pretty much impossible to determine his levels of the physical disciplines, but he clearly has all three in some measure. In CofD, he'd presumably have all three of the standard Coils at high levels, considering he allegedly invented them; Ascendant in particular he either has above 5 or has some kind of crazy Scale for, because he walks in the sun unprotected and unharmed, if perhaps not at full strength. And that's just his Disciplines. I'm pretty sure he'd easily break 500 experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would add that coils that makes you &quot;one with the land&quot; (its from the 1k Nights book) which sound very draculaish. The rest depends on what Dracula, i would say the blood armor devotion is must because i love that movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-27-2017, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T00:18:22-07:00","id":1121214,"title":"","content":"This is my personal view according with book and movie:<br /> <br /> Int 4 wits 5 resolve 5<br /> Strenght 6 dex 3 stam 3<br /> Pres 5 manip 5 comp 4<br /> <br /> Animal ken 5<br /> Weapon. 6/7<br /> Persuasion 5<br /> Other skill...<br /> <br /> Protean 5<br /> Animalism 5<br /> Vigor 4<br /> Celerity 3<br /> Resilence 4<br /> Dominate 3<br /> Obfuscate 5<br /> Majesty 2<br /> Auspex 5<br /> Nightmare 4<br /> Coil of the Voivode 5<br /> Coil of the Ascendant 5<br /> Coil of the wyrm 5<br /> Coil of Zinitra 5<br /> <br /> Devotion:<br /> <br /> Force of Nature","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T05:48:45-07:00","id":1121271,"title":"","content":"Should Dracula not be last of Pijavica Clan members?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T05:56:37-07:00","id":1121274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula?p=1121271#post1121271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Dracula not be last of Pijavica Clan members?</div> </div> </div> </div>No? He's not known for being a puddle of blood at any point. Gangrel is probably the best fit for his Clan if you're going to give him one, though there are a lot of good reasons to believe he's probably clanless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T06:51:16-07:00","id":1121283,"title":"","content":"Continuing the &quot;Clanless&quot; train of thought, the account of his final battle in Rites could actually be interpreted as him being a Revenant. I know the Coil of Blood isn't canon any more, but s Revenant's hunger would make a great impetus for him to have developed a Coil based around lessening reliance on feeding. He could also easily be a Neglatu and the brides his brood. That would explain his having rumored to have &quot;embraced&quot; them into different Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-27-2017, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T07:18:15-07:00","id":1121297,"title":"","content":"So, another potentially pertinent thought. Secrets of the Covenants has an astoundingly atmospheric fluff piece on the Brides and Dracula which suggests some very interesting things about him and the Coils. Part of which could also be interpreted for him originally being a Revenant or a Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T09:35:43-07:00","id":1121348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula?p=1121283#post1121283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Continuing the &quot;Clanless&quot; train of thought, the account of his final battle in Rites could actually be interpreted as him being a Revenant. I know the Coil of Blood isn't canon any more, but s Revenant's hunger would make a great impetus for him to have developed a Coil based around lessening reliance on feeding. He could also easily be a Neglatu and the brides his brood. That would explain his having rumored to have &quot;embraced&quot; them into different Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, Drakula being Neglatu and extending his evolution from it to 'transtendental vampires' of Ordo Dracul is greatest head canon I read on <b>Vampire</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thank you, Willow! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:07:14-07:00","id":1121359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula?p=1121283#post1121283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Continuing the &quot;Clanless&quot; train of thought, the account of his final battle in Rites could actually be interpreted as him being a Revenant. I know the Coil of Blood isn't canon any more, but s Revenant's hunger would make a great impetus for him to have developed a Coil based around lessening reliance on feeding. He could also easily be a Neglatu and the brides his brood. That would explain his having rumored to have &quot;embraced&quot; them into different Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it more - with reading of <b>Lancea Sanctum</b> book - 'Neglatu Theory' also nice answers Longinus. He was ever hungry Revenant <i>until</i> he meet Vahishtael.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:28:35-07:00","id":1121488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula?p=1121348#post1121348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, Drakula being Neglatu and extending his evolution from it to 'transtendental vampires' of Ordo Dracul is greatest head canon I read on <b>Vampire</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thank you, Willow! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's some high praise! Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T20:49:21-07:00","id":1121693,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Dracula could be any clan, or none. If you interpret Dracula as a metaphor for animal savagery and atavistic tendencies in the subconscious, he's Gangrel. Is he a metaphor for sexual predators or the alluring dangers of breaking from cultural sexual mores? He's a Daeva. An embodiment of the dangers of a rampant aristocracy/upper class? He's a Ventrue. Metaphor for disease, embodiment of everything that we fear lurks in the shadows of the world and our minds? He's a Nosferatu. The dangers of too much knowledge and hidden, insidious threats? Mekhet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T03:43:53-07:00","id":1121770,"title":"","content":"I'd stat Dracula depending on what role he'd have in the chronicle. He's gonna be exceptional no matter what since he managed to create the Coils without prior knowledge of them (in contrast to those who create new Coils knowing it's actually possible), but he might not be ungodly powerful just because he's a vampire genius.<br /> My three takes are these:<br /> \u2022 A pretty good Gangrel. Exceptional compared to his contemporaries, but gonna have trouble if he ever went toe-to-toe with a truly ancient being like the Unholy. May or may not have started as a revenant first.<br /> \u2022 A revenant who managed to uplift himself (probably to Gangrel but doesn't matter in modern nights), and then managed to use his mastery of the Coils to uplift himself again to being Clanless. 1E had ideas about Coils having an additional dot that represented true mastery of it, and I recall a six dot Threnody that supposedly could turn someone Clanless. It seems fitting that beyond normal mastery of a power that actually changes the vampire template should be able to remove the clan.<br /> \u2022 The vampire equivalent of an archmage. He didn't just discover that the Coils are possible and lay the groundwork for others to build on top. He created the possibility of developing Coils. Without his intervention Coils neither would nor could exist. If I'd stat someone like that I'd probably play around with the vampire template as whole and quite possibly add the archmaster bonus of always winning Clashes of Wills against lower beings.<br /> <br /> While it's certainly tempting to stat him as a vampire god, I think there's a charm to having him be a genius but ultimately still a normal vampire (except from the Coils he's learned during the years).<br /> But it's all up to what's fitting for the chronicle. In our current vampire campaign (where I'm a player) I'd actually be disappointed if he wasn't some sort of super vampire, just because that's how high powered this campaign is. We've already met the Unholy, had direct dealings with the Crone, and fought the JoJo-posing guy on page 120 in Shadows of Mexico. A mundane Dracula would be a total letdown by this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:37:55-07:00","id":1121909,"title":"","content":"Why am I statting him and what literary or pop culture interpretations am I using.<br /> <br /> Pseudo historical rendering of Vlad Tepes - A highly intelligent Ventrue hyper specialized in the mental side of politics but rather deficit in the social side of politics and super powers department<br /> Bram Stoker's version - a moderately intelligent Daeva who developed a few devotions <br /> Pop culture - knock offs from a video game, anime, comics, World of Darkness RPGs. A dumber than dirt Gangrel Mary Sue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T10:37:15-07:00","id":1121951,"title":"","content":"Personally, if Dracula was showing up in my Chronicle then he'd be a Bela Lugosi knock off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:34:34-07:00","id":1122408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121176-how-to-stat-dracula?p=1121909#post1121909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why am I statting him and what literary or pop culture interpretations am I using.<br /> <br /> Pseudo historical rendering of Vlad Tepes - A highly intelligent Ventrue hyper specialized in the mental side of politics but rather deficit in the social side of politics and super powers department<br /> Bram Stoker's version - a moderately intelligent Daeva who developed a few devotions<br /> Pop culture - knock offs from a video game, anime, comics, World of Darkness RPGs. A dumber than dirt Gangrel Mary Sue</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with Stoker's original Dracula being a Daeva. He is portrayed as a very hairy and decidedly unattractive man. Sex symbol, he ain't. Not quite to the levels of ugliness that <i>Nosferatu </i>would take him via the character of Count Orlok, though. We never see Dracula use supernatural quickness, or supernatural attractiveness. Powers that he exhibits throughout the book can be summed up with: Animalism, Dominate, Protean, Vigor. Applying Occam's Razor to his stats, it's actually easiest to say that he's a Julii with an unusual bloodline, perhaps one that emerged on the borders of Dacia and Thrace in response to the difficulties of enforcing the Pax Romana in the South Slavic world...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T12:59:22-07:00","id":1122441,"title":"","content":"Stoker's Dracula would definitely not be a Daeva. Daeva's defining characteristic is passion, and that's not a major defining characteristic of Dracula in the novel (though it is in a lot of modern interpretations of the source material that try to romanticize his relationship with Mina). He isn't defined by fear or mystery for me either, so I'd rule out Mekhet and Nosferatu. That leaves either Ventrue or Gangrel, as power and instinct are both important characteristics of his. It's also appropriate that those be the two he's split between, given that they're so closely associated in the lore, and the fact that his two most famous abilities - shapeshifting and mind control - are the signature abilities of both Clans. They also share another of his better-known powers, control of animals. Personally, I interpret book Dracula as a very Ventrue-like Gangrel, though vice-versa would also work for me. He could even belong to a much older Bloodline that eventually separated off of Gangrel into the Ventrue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}